IceStorm subscriber in a private network, reachable only through Glacier2.

- public: IceStorm, Glacier2 and the publisher
- private: the subscriber, that only sees Glacier2

compose.yml simulates both networks. Glacier2 is attached to both of them, as a
firewall with two interfaces. The subscriber creates a Glacier2 session and
registers its servant in an object adapter bound to the router: IceStorm sends
the events to Glacier2, that forwards them through the connection opened by the
subscriber.

Procedure:

  $ make up        # start icestorm, glacier2 and the subscriber
  $ make logs      # keep it open to see the events
  $ make publish   # (in other terminal) publish 10 events
  $ make down
